message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  A reservoir-coupled therapeutic interfering particle can assist immune-mediated
  HIV-1 post-treatment control: a within-host modeling study
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, self-audited within-host modeling study extending Dodd & de Boer (2025)
  into the latent-reservoir / analytical-treatment-interruption (ATI) setting. A therapeutic
  interfering particle (TIP) coupled to reservoir reactivation is predicted to assist (not
  antagonize) immune-mediated post-treatment control; a non-coupled TIP recovers the de Boer
  active-infection limit. The effect is robust across global parameter sampling and three
  immune models, never backfires, and is explained by a derived effective reproduction number.
  Illustrative modeling hypothesis, not validated experimental findings.
